            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 30-year-old female, admitted on 29/11/2011 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. Diagnostic workup included physical examination, blood tests revealing leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound confirming appendiceal inflammation. Given the clear clinical and imaging findings, the patient underwent laparoscopic appendectomy on 29/11/2011 without intraoperative complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Pain management and intravenous fluid replacement were administered throughout the stay. Wound care was provided prior to discharge. The patient was discharged home on 01/12/2011 in good general condition with instructions regarding wound care and follow-up. Please arrange outpatient follow-up within two weeks. Should any concerns arise, do not hesitate to contact our department.</div>"
            },
